}
```

The exception is caught, both catch blocks empty, then control reaches `}` without returning → UBSan "execution reached the end of a value-returning function without returning a value" — this is a fatal runtime error under OSS-Fuzz UBSan config (which uses `-fsanitize=fuzzer,address,undefined` and UBSan reports lead to abort by default in fuzzing mode? Actually UBSan continues by default but prints report; libFuzzer treats any sanitizer report as a crash since it sets `halt_on_error=1` ... For detecting: UBSan emits report and the `__ubsan_handle_..._abort` variants are used when `-fno-sanitize-recover=all` is set, which IS the OSS-Fuzz default? OSS-Fuzz default is `-fsanitize=address` for C/C++ with `-fno-sanitize-recover=all`... hmm, actually the CFLAGS in OSS-Fuzz include `-fsanitize=address` typically, but for ubsan builds it uses `-fsanitize=array-bounds,bool,builtin,enum,float-divide-by-zero,function,integer-divide-by-zero,null,object-size,return,returns-nonnull-attribute,shift,signed-integer-overflow,unsigned-integer-overflow,unreachable,vla-bound,vptr -fno-sanitize-recover=array-bounds,...` including `return`. The "return" check is included in the OSS-Fuzz UBSan list with `-fno-sanitize-recover` covering it → abort on error.

